course: dictionary
lesson: 6176
title: Minority: the smaller part
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A minority is the smaller number or part of a group, less than half. Look at the words around it to find out. «If 8 of 30 pupils like sprouts, they are a minority.» Eight is fewer than half of thirty, so those eight pupils are the minority.
explain: The word can also name a group of people who are different from most people in a country, for example in their language, religion or culture. «China also has 55 officially recognised minorities.» The clue is «majority people», who are the big group, so minorities must be the smaller groups.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in «smaller part» and reading the sentence again. «Majority rule must still protect the rights of the minority.» The smaller part still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Majority and minority are opposites.
fact: Minority means less than half of a group.
fact: The opposite of minority is majority, which means more than half.
fact: «A small minority» means only a few people out of the whole group.
fact: A minority language is a language spoken by a smaller group of people in a country.
fact: In law, minority also means the time when a person is still a child, usually under eighteen in most places.
exercise: Why are the 8 pupils who like sprouts called a minority? | They are the biggest group in the class | They are the teacher's favourite | They are all the same age | * They are fewer than half of the 30 pupils
exercise: Which word in «Majority rule must still protect the rights of the minority» is the opposite of minority? | protect | rights | rule | * majority
exercise: Which phrase means only a few people out of the whole group? | A large majority | * A small minority | A loud shout | A happy crowd
test: «Only 12 of 40 children have a pet dog.» Are the dog owners the majority or the minority? | Neither, because there is no number to check | * Minority | Majority | Both at once
test: «The minority loses but should still be respected.» What does this teach us about voting? | The minority always wins the vote | Only the majority has any rights | Voting is not fair at all | * The minority should still be respected even when it loses
exam: «The majority must still protect the minority.» What does minority mean here? | * The smaller group, fewer than half | A rule about voting | A school sports team | The bigger group, more than half
